[5.09,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your AWS account (region eu-south-2); ov runs none of them:\r\n\r\n  # SSH access: the key pair for this stack (.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345-key.pem), its public half imported here.\r\n  aws ec2 import-key-pair --key-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345-key --public-key-material fileb://.openvidu/aws/openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345-key.pub --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the elastic topology,\r\n  # and its parameters, written out for you to read (the parameters file is 0600: it\r\n  # carries the license, which on the command line any user of this machine would see):\r\n  #   .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-elastic.yaml\r\n  #   .openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json\r\n  # CloudFormation takes a template this size from S3: stage it in a bucket of your\r\n  # account, created once and reused by every stack.\r\n  BUCKET=\"openvidu-cfn-templates-$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text --region eu-south-2)-eu-south-2\"\r\n  aws s3api head-bucket --bucket $BUCKET --region eu-south-2 2>/dev/null || aws s3api create-bucket --bucket $BUCKET --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=eu-south-2 --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # The network the stack goes into (the template creates none):\r\n  #   the region's default VPC, vpc-0e2358cb016b9fef5, and its default subnets: subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a), subnet-02776aa519c2198f1 (eu-south-2b), subnet-0053e4f7269e42ebc (eu-south-2c)\r\n  #   the master in subnet-0497cd2d92bbfd794 (eu-south-2a); the media nodes in all of them\r\n\r\n  # Create the machines. DeployedBy=instance: master-1 installs OpenVidu with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI and the other nodes join it, so the stack is serving shortly after\r\n  # CloudFormation finishes. `deploy` returns when CloudFormation is done (about 7 minutes).\r\n  aws cloudformation deploy --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345 --template-file .openvidu/aws/cf-openvidu-pro-elastic.yaml --capabilities CAPABILITY_IAM CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM --no-fail-on-empty-changeset --s3-bucket $BUCKET --s3-prefix openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345 --parameter-overrides file://.openvidu/aws/cfn-parameters.json --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\n  # Read back where the stack is and what it published: URL, credentials and the\r\n  # stack's access (KUBECONFIG is \"none\" until OpenVidu is up). The secret's name\r\n  # is the stack's SharedInfoSecret output.\r\n  aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345 --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs' --output json --region eu-south-2\r\n  SECRET=\"$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345 --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='\\''SharedInfoSecret'\\''].OutputValue' --output text --region eu-south-2)\"\r\n  aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id $SECRET --query SecretString --output text --region eu-south-2\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-aws-el-s094345 --cloud aws --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
